window.LXD.body.en={"acc-reports": "You can find the reports in the **Accounting** section. They can be filtered by company, period, and Cost Center, and exported to Excel or PDF.\n\n| Report | Answers |\n|---|---|\n| Trial Balance | Are the books balanced? And the balances of all accounts |\n| Income Statement | Income, expenses, and profit in a period |\n| Balance Sheet | Assets, liabilities, and equity at a date |\n| Cash Flow | Where the cash came from and where it went |\n| General Ledger | All movements of a specific account |\n| Customer / Supplier Account Statement | What is owed to them and by them |\n| Accounts Receivable Ageing | Overdue invoices and how long they are overdue |\n\n## Tips\n\n- Always open a report with a specific period, then compare it with a previous period.\n- Click any number to drill down to the documents that make it up.\n- Save the most-used reports as a shortcut on your home page.\n- Use Cost Centers to compare the profitability of branches.", "ai": "LedgerX Assistant is a round icon at the bottom corner of every screen (desktop, CRM and HR). Click it, ask in Arabic or English, and it explains how any page works or builds a report from your data. It can read and explain only: it never creates, changes or deletes anything. It tells you the steps to do that yourself.\n\n## What you can ask\n\n- **How things work**: \"How do I create a sales invoice?\", \"What does the Journal Entry page do?\". It answers from this guide.\n- **Reports**: \"Total sales this month\", \"Top 10 customers\", \"Sales per month this year\", \"Open purchase orders\". Answers come as a table in the chat. Use the **Excel** button on a table to download it, and ask for a chart (\"as a chart\") to see a simple bar, line or pie chart.\n- **A record**: \"Show invoice SINV-0001\".\n- **The page you are on**: \"Explain this page\". The assistant knows which page is open.\n\n## Permissions\n\nThe assistant works with your own permissions, exactly like you: your roles, your user permissions and your field-level access. If you ask about something you are not allowed to see, it replies **\"This is outside your permissions\"** and shows nothing about it. It also does not explain guide pages of modules you do not have. Passwords, keys and tokens are never shown to anyone through it.\n\n## Set up (administrator)\n\n1. Create an API key in the Claude console (console.anthropic.com).\n2. Open **LedgerX AI Settings** from the search bar. Paste the key in **Claude API Key** (it is stored encrypted and never shown again), tick **Enabled** and save.\n3. Optional: choose the model, the daily question limit per user, the largest table size, a role that may use it, and extra notes about your business.\n4. Refresh the page. The icon appears for the users who are allowed.\n\nEvery question is recorded in **LedgerX AI Log** (who asked, the question, the answer, the size). Only a System Manager can open it.\n\n## Good to know\n\n- Each question is sent to Claude (Anthropic) together with the parts of your data it needs to answer, and the provider bills the API usage to your key. Do not enable it if your policy forbids sending business data to an external service.\n- Check important numbers against the standard reports before you act on them. The assistant can misread a question; it states the filters it used so you can see them.\n- If the key is rejected or the server has no internet, the chat says so in one line.", "buying": "## The purchasing cycle\n\nMaterial Request ← Supplier Quotation ← Purchase Order ← Purchase Receipt ← Purchase Invoice ← Payment Entry.\n\n## Material Request and supplier quotations\n\nAny department records its need in a **Material Request**. From the request, requests for quotation are created for several Suppliers, the prices are compared, and the best one is chosen.\n\n## Purchase Order\n\nIt is sent to the Supplier with the quantities, prices, and supply dates. It can be emailed directly from the system.\n\n## Receipt and invoice\n\n- The **Purchase Receipt** brings the goods into the Warehouse with the actual quantity.\n- The **Purchase Invoice** records your obligation to the Supplier. It can be created from the receipt.\n- The system matches the invoice with the order and the receipt.\n\n## Payment\n\nFrom the Purchase Invoice create a Payment Entry, or pay several invoices to the Supplier at once from a direct **Payment Entry**.\n\n## Reports\n\nPayables ageing, purchases by Supplier and Item, and orders overdue for supply.", "coa": "## The idea\n\nThe Chart of Accounts is the structure of the company's books. It is divided into five main roots: Assets, Liabilities, Equity, Income, and Expenses. **Group** accounts contain sub-accounts, and **ledger** accounts are the ones entries are posted to.\n\n## Adding an account\n\n1. Open the **Chart of Accounts** and choose the company.\n2. Click the parent account, then **Add Child**.\n3. Set the name, the type (Bank, Cash, Receivable, Payable, Tax, Expense...), and the currency.\n\n## Important account types\n\n| Type | Use |\n|---|---|\n| Cash / Bank | Cash boxes and bank accounts, and they appear in Payment Entries |\n| Receivable / Payable | Customer and Supplier accounts, set automatically in invoices |\n| Tax | VAT accounts and other taxes |\n| Stock | Inventory value, updated automatically by Item movements |\n| Expense / Cost of Goods Sold | Charged on sale or issue |\n\n## Tips\n\n- Keep the numbering organized so it is easy to refer back to.\n- Do not create an account for every Customer: the general Receivable account is enough, and the account statement is produced per Customer.\n- Before actual posting, review the chart with your certified accountant.", "company": "## Creating the company\n\nFrom the **Company** menu, add a new company and set:\n\n- **Name and abbreviation**: the abbreviation is used in account and Warehouse names.\n- **Default currency**: the currency of the company's books. It is hard to change once entries exist.\n- **Country**: determines the default taxes and templates.\n- **Chart of Accounts**: choose a ready-made template or create it from scratch.\n\nWhen you save, the system creates the basic accounts, Warehouses, and default Cost Centers.\n\n## Fiscal Year\n\nCreate a Fiscal Year with a start date and an end date. An entry cannot be posted outside a defined Fiscal Year. At the end of the year you can close it with a closing entry, and the remaining balances carry over automatically to the next year.\n\n## Multiple branches and companies\n\n- **Separate companies**: each company has its own books and reports, and they can be consolidated in combined reports.\n- **Branches within a company**: use Cost Centers and Warehouses, and restrict users with User Permissions.\n\n> ! Do not delete a company that has entries. Disable it instead.", "concepts": "Understanding these few terms makes the rest of the guide easier.\n\n## The document (DocType)\n\nEvery type of record in the system is called a \"document\": Sales Invoice, Customer, employee, asset, and so on. Each type has an entry form, a list, reports, and permissions.\n\n## Document states\n\n| State | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| Draft | Editable and has no effect on accounts or inventory |\n| Submitted | Posted: entries and inventory are affected, and it cannot be edited directly |\n| Cancelled | Its effect is reversed, and it stays in the record for review |\n\n> To correct a submitted document, cancel it, then amend it and submit it again, or create a return.\n\n## Linking documents\n\nAn invoice can be created from a sales order, and a sales order from a quotation. The **Create** button at the top of a document shows the next documents in the cycle, and the data is carried over to them automatically. In each document you will find a **Connections** panel that shows everything linked to it.\n\n## Company and Cost Center\n\nA company is an independent accounting entity. A Cost Center distributes expenses and revenues across branches, departments, and projects.\n\n## Roles and permissions\n\nEach user has Roles that determine what they can see and do. You can restrict a user to a company, a branch, or a Warehouse through **User Permissions**.\n\n## Workspaces\n\nEach module has a home page with shortcuts, reports, and number cards. You can find the modules from the home screen or from the sidebar.", "crm": "The CRM application follows a customer from first contact to a won deal. It opens from the **CRM** tile and runs on its own screen, in the same colours and language as the rest of the system.\n\n## Leads\n\nA Lead is a person or company that showed interest: name, organization, email, mobile, source and owner. Add leads by hand, import them from Excel (**Import**), or let them arrive on their own: the online store's contact form and its test-drive and booking requests create a lead with source **Website**. View leads as a list or as a **Kanban** board by status.\n\n## Deals\n\nWhen a lead is serious, press **Convert to Deal**. A Deal has a status, an expected closing date, a probability, a value and a list of **Products** with quantities. Move it between statuses; **Won** and **Lost** close it. A lost deal asks for the reason.\n\n## Activities and follow-up\n\nEvery lead and deal keeps its own timeline: notes, tasks, calls, emails and comments. Assign tasks with a due date so the whole team sees what is next. **Call Logs** lists the calls.\n\n## Organizations and contacts\n\nA deal belongs to an **Organization** and has one or more **Contacts**. They are kept once and reused across deals.\n\n## Link to accounting\n\n- When a deal reaches the chosen status (by default **Won**), the CRM creates the **Customer** in the accounting module, with its contacts and address. From the deal you can also create a **Quotation**.\n- The link is switched on for you when the Fleet app is installed. An administrator can change which status creates the customer, or switch the link off.\n- Fleet adds two buttons to the deal page: **Create Rental Contract** and **Create Fleet Trip**, filled with the deal's customer.\n- Showroom adds a **Car of Interest** field to leads and deals, in the side panel.\n- The Operations Research module reads open deals (their products, probability and closing date) as expected demand in the Reorder Plan and the Product Mix Plan.\n\n## Dashboard\n\nThe **Dashboard** shows total leads, ongoing and won deals, average deal values, the sales trend, forecasted revenue, funnel conversion, deals by stage, territory, source and salesperson, leads by source, and lost-deal reasons. Choose the period and the user at the top.", "education": "A single module for managing education from nursery to university with a flexible structure: schools with stages, grades, and classes, and universities with faculties, departments, and years.\n\n## Main sections\n\n| Area | What it includes |\n|---|---|\n| Admissions and students | Admission applications, student and guardian, siblings, transfer |\n| Fees and accounts | Fee structures, sibling discount, fee installments, collection and invoices |\n| Academic | Subjects, timetables, attendance, exams, grades, cumulative GPA |\n| Staff | Teachers and faculty members and their workloads |\n\n## Fees\n\nDefine a **Fee Structure** for each stage, then create an **installment schedule** for the student with due dates. Sibling discounts are calculated automatically, and a Sales Invoice is created in the guardian's name.\n\n## Attendance and alerts\n\nEach class's daily attendance is recorded, the attendance percentage is calculated, and **absence alerts** are sent daily to guardians.\n\n## Grades\n\nExam weights and the grading scale are calculated automatically, and a **student result certificate** is issued. In universities the cumulative GPA is calculated.\n\n## Reports\n\nFees due, class density, attendance summary, result certificate, and fee collection.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Fees are recorded as revenue at invoicing, without deferral over the study months.\n- Bulk end-of-year promotion is not yet available.", "einvoicing": "The E-Invoicing app sends your Sales Invoices to a tax system and keeps the answer on the invoice. Find it on the desktop as the **E-Invoicing** tile (route `/desk/e-invoicing`). It works for **Egypt** (Tax Authority), **Saudi Arabia** (ZATCA / Fatoora), the **UAE** (Peppol through an accredited service provider) and, through a configurable connector, any other system in any country.\n\n## Set up once\n\n1. **E-Invoice Connection**: one per company. Choose the system and the environment (start with Test), and fill the seller block: tax number, commercial register, address. It must match what the authority has on file.\n2. On every **Item** set the e-invoice code and type; on every **UOM** the unit code; on the **Customer** the tax number and buyer type.\n3. Egypt: client id and secret from the taxpayer portal, the activity code and a signing service for the digital seal. Saudi: press the four onboarding steps. UAE: your provider's address and credentials. Other countries: choose **Custom API** and describe the request.\n\n## Sending\n\nWhen a Sales Invoice (or a return, which is sent as a credit note) is submitted, the app creates an **E-Invoice Submission** and sends it in the background. The invoice shows the status and the authority's reference. If the system is down the app tries again every 10 minutes. On the invoice, **E-Invoicing > Preview E-Invoice** shows exactly what would be sent, and **Send to the Tax Authority** sends it by hand.\n\nThe submission keeps the request and the answer. Statuses: Pending, Submitted (received, waiting for validation), Accepted, Rejected (fix the data and **Send Again**), Failed (technical problem, retried), Cancelled. The report **Unsent E-Invoices** lists invoices that were not accepted yet.\n\n## Cancelling\n\nEgypt: cancelling the invoice cancels it at the authority first (within the period the authority allows). Saudi Arabia and the UAE do not allow cancelling a sent invoice: the app stops the cancel and you issue a credit note.\n\n## Saudi onboarding\n\nOn the connection, in order: **1. Generate Certificate Request**, type the one-time code from the portal, **2. Get Compliance Certificate**, **3. Run Compliance Checks**, **4. Get Production Certificate**. Do all of this on Simulation first.\n\n## Important\n\nThe app follows the authorities' published specifications and is tested with simulated answers. Run it against each authority's test environment and fix any difference before sending real invoices.", "factory": "Manufacturing is a standalone module with its own **Factory** tile on the desktop. It holds production, quality, reports and setup in one place, with barcode scanning for operations, stages and production lines.\n\n## Sections\n\n| Section | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| Production | Work Orders, Job Cards, Production Plan, BOMs, the operator screen, the scan log |\n| Quality | Quality Inspection, Non Conformance, Actions, Goals, Reviews, Feedback, Procedures and Templates |\n| Reports | Line Efficiency, Waste, Operator Productivity, Production Cost, and the standard manufacturing reports |\n| Setup | Production Lines, Workstations, Operations, Routings, Waste Reasons, Factory Settings |\n\n## Production lines and stations\n\nCreate a **Production Line**, add its stations in order and set the target output per hour. Every station and every line gets a barcode automatically.\n\n## Operator screen\n\nOpen `/factory` on a phone or a scanner PC:\n\n1. Scan the **employee badge** (employee ID or badge code), then the **station barcode**.\n2. Scan the **Job Card**: the required and completed quantities appear.\n3. Press **Start**; you can **Pause** and **Resume**.\n4. Press **Finish** and enter the good quantity, the scrap and its reason.\n5. When the whole quantity is done the Job Card is submitted automatically; if a quality inspection is needed you see why.\n\nAny scanner that types the code and presses Enter works; Chrome on Android can scan with the camera. A code like `ITEM*12` means quantity 12.\n\n## Materials and finished product\n\nOpen a **Work Order** by scanning it: scan the raw materials and the system checks they belong to the BOM and do not exceed the required quantity, then press **Post Material Issue**. To receive the product enter the quantity and press **Receive Finished Product**.\n\n## Quality\n\n- Turn on **Quality inspection required** on the operation in the Work Order, or make it a rule for every Job Card in **Factory Settings**.\n- The **Quality Check** button on the screen creates the inspection and opens its link.\n\n## Waste and cost\n\nScrap is recorded with the Job Card and its reason. The **Production Cost** report shows materials, operating cost and the actual unit cost against the BOM cost.\n\n## Printing labels\n\nFrom a Job Card, Work Order, Workstation, Employee or Item form: **Barcode -> Print Barcode Label**. From a list, select several records and print them together.\n\n> ! Material issue and receipt use the standard Stock Entries, so any rule there (batches, serial numbers, required Job Cards) shows up as it is.", "faq": "## I don't see a new module after the update\n\nRun the migration and clear the cache, then refresh the browser with `Ctrl + Shift + R`. Make sure the user has a Role that allows the module.\n\n## I can't edit a document\n\nA submitted document cannot be edited. Cancel it and then amend it, or create a return or an adjustment entry.\n\n## The numbers in the report don't match my expectation\n\nCheck the company, period, and Cost Center in the filters, and that all documents are **submitted**, not draft.\n\n## An error message when saving\n\nRead the text of the message, as it usually names the missing field or the incorrect account. If the cause isn't clear, copy it and send it to the system administrator.\n\n## How do I change the language\n\nFrom **My Settings**, or from the language switcher on the login page.\n\n## How do I search for anything\n\n`Ctrl + K` inside the system. In this guide too, `Ctrl + K`.\n\n## How do I print this guide or save it as a PDF\n\nClick the download icon at the top of the page and choose **Save as PDF** from the print dialog.", "features": "## Accounting\n\n- A flexible Chart of Accounts, multi-company and multi-currency.\n- Sales and purchase invoices, payments, receipt and payment vouchers, cheques.\n- Taxes (VAT and others) and automatic entries.\n- Cost Centers and budgets.\n- Trial balance, income statement, balance sheet, cash flow.\n\n## Sales and purchasing\n\n- Quotations, sales orders, delivery notes, invoices, returns.\n- Purchase requests, supplier quotations, purchase orders, receipts.\n- Price lists, discounts, payment schedules, and installments.\n\n## Inventory\n\n- Multiple Warehouses with balance tracking and transfers.\n- Serial numbers, batches, and expiry dates.\n- Periodic stock counts and inventory valuation.\n\n## Customers\n\n- Leads, sales opportunities, and follow-up activities.\n- Direct link to quotations and invoices.\n\n## Human resources\n\n- Employee files, attendance, leave, advances.\n- Payroll, salary components, and deductions.\n\n## Specialized modules\n\nFleet, field sales, payment network, hotels, car showroom, education, real estate development. You can find an explanation of each module in the **LedgerX modules** section.\n\n## User experience\n\n- Quick search, and a home screen with an icon for each module.\n- Dashboards, number cards, and charts.\n- Excel export and import, and printing in professional formats.\n- Works on computer and mobile.", "fieldsales": "The sales representative's mobile screen: route, customers, debts, selling from the vehicle Warehouse, collection, and handing over custody.\n\n## The representative's day\n\n1. **Start of day**: the representative sees their route, their Customers, and the Customers' debts.\n2. **The visit**: they record their arrival at the Customer by geographic location.\n3. **Selling**: they sell from the vehicle Warehouse, so quantities decrease and the invoice is created.\n4. **Collection**: they receive cash or deposit in the bank, and it is recorded on the Customer's account.\n5. **Closing the day**: they hand over the cash, and the day is closed with hours and sales calculated.\n\n## Link to human resources\n\n- The representative is linked to the driver and the employee through the same user.\n- The first attendance record or sale of the day marks the employee as **present**.\n- At the start of each month, a draft **Additional Salary** with last month's commission is created for each representative, without duplication.\n\n## Settings\n\nFrom **Field Sales Settings** set the company, the Warehouses, the accounts, and the commission component.\n\n> There is a short Arabic guide for the representative inside the module.", "fleet": "Complete fleet management, from a few cars to a multi-branch fleet. It extends the existing vehicle and driver records without altering them.\n\n## What the module covers\n\n| Area | Records |\n|---|---|\n| Foundation | Vehicle, driver, vehicle type, driver assignment, fleet documents (license and insurance) with expiry alerts, tires |\n| Maintenance | Maintenance plans, maintenance schedules by kilometers or days, work orders (tasks, parts, and labor), fuel log |\n| Operations | Trips, rental contracts, traffic violations, accidents |\n| Tracking | GPS devices and vehicle locations |\n\n## Daily use\n\n1. Add the vehicles and drivers and assign them.\n2. Record each vehicle's documents with their expiry dates, and you will get a daily alert before expiry.\n3. Create a maintenance plan and apply it, and **Due Soon** and **Overdue** will appear.\n4. Record fuel fill-ups so the system calculates consumption per 100 km.\n5. Create a **Trip** with its expenses and revenue, and invoice the Customer for it.\n6. For rental: create a **Rental Contract** with several vehicles and free kilometers, and the excess and damages will be calculated and the invoice created.\n\n## Violations\n\nA violation is charged to the company, the driver, or the Customer. If it is charged to a driver, it can be deducted from their salary.\n\n## Reports\n\nDocument expiry, maintenance due dates, vehicle cost, fuel consumption, and trip profitability.\n\n## Roles\n\nThe **Fleet Manager** has all permissions. The **Fleet Operator** only records trips and fuel.", "hotels": "Hotel management that starts from a small guesthouse and reaches a full resort.\n\n## Rooms and reservations\n\n- **Hotels, room types, and rooms**, with a housekeeping status (clean, dirty, maintenance, out of service).\n- **Double-booking prevention**: when a reservation is confirmed, every night is reserved for the room, so two people cannot book the same room for the same night, even at the same moment.\n\n## Rates and offers\n\nSeasonal rate plans for each room type, a meal plan (room only, with breakfast, half board, full board, all inclusive), rates for the public, corporates, and agents, a weekend surcharge, a minimum number of nights, and promo codes. A stay that crosses two seasons is priced night by night.\n\n## Folio and accounts\n\nThe **Folio** collects room nights, meals, and services with service charges and VAT and tourism taxes. On checkout an invoice is created from which advance payments are deducted. Corporate and agent reservations can be left open and invoiced monthly.\n\n## Currencies\n\nThe invoice is in one currency, but the guest can pay in any accepted currency, and each payment is created at the exchange rate of its day.\n\n## Cancellation policy\n\nFree cancellation up to a number of days before arrival, then a percentage of the first night. A no-show is charged the first night.\n\n## Optional sections\n\nFrom **Hotel Settings ← Sections** enable only what you operate: restaurants and bars, activities and services, group bookings, housekeeping and maintenance. Each outlet (restaurant, spa, beach...) has a revenue account, a Cost Center, and a Warehouse.\n\n## Integration\n\nGuests are Customers in the system, so the CRM team sees them, and airport pickup can be linked to a vehicle from the fleet.\n\n## Reports\n\nArrivals and departures, occupancy, and open invoices.", "hr": "## Employee file\n\nRecord personal data, job, department, direct manager, salary data, bank account, and documents. Link the employee to a system user so they can log in themselves.\n\n## Attendance and leave\n\n- **Attendance**: manual, by check-in and check-out system, or from mobile.\n- **Leave**: types, balances, annual cycles, and request and manager approval.\n- **Holidays**: a holiday list that is excluded from the calculation.\n\n## Shifts\n\nDefine shifts and schedule them for employees, and lateness and overtime are calculated from them.\n\n## Payroll\n\n1. Define the **Salary Components** (basic, allowances, deductions, insurance, taxes).\n2. Create a **Salary Structure** for each category and assign it to the employee.\n3. Run **Payroll Entry** for the month, and it calculates attendance and leave.\n4. Review the slips and submit them, and the payroll entry is created.\n\n## Advances and additions\n\nAn **Employee Advance** is deducted in installments from the salary. An **Additional Salary** adds or deducts an amount for a single month, such as commissions and penalties.\n\n## Reports\n\nSalary register, monthly attendance, leave balances, and employee cost per department.", "install": "> This page is for the system administrator.\n\n## Updating\n\n```\ncd <bench-folder>/apps/<app-name>\ngit pull origin main\ncd <bench-folder>\nbench --site mysite.localhost migrate\nbench --site mysite.localhost clear-cache\n```\n\nThen restart the services and refresh the browser by pressing `Ctrl + Shift + R`.\n\n## Installing a new module\n\n1. Copy the app to the apps folder.\n2. Add it to the apps list and install it with the Python package.\n3. Install it on the site, then run the migration and clear the cache.\n4. Do a full restart.\n\n> ! If you add the app to the list without copying and installing it, the server will not work. Verify that all the steps are complete.\n\n## Backup\n\nRun `bench --site mysite.localhost backup --with-files` regularly and keep the copies off the server.\n\n## First steps when there are problems\n\n- Open the **Error Log** from the system and copy the error text.\n- Try clearing the cache and restarting.\n- Check that all modules are installed on the site.", "invoices": "## Sales Invoice\n\n1. Open a new **Sales Invoice** (or create it from a sales order).\n2. Choose the Customer, and the terms and address are filled in automatically.\n3. Add the Items and quantities, and the price will be calculated from the Price List.\n4. Add tax and discount if any.\n5. **Save** then **Submit**.\n\nOn submission, the receivable, revenue, and tax entries are created, and the goods leave the inventory if you enabled stock update.\n\n## Payment schedule and installments\n\nIn the invoice there is a **Payment Terms** table: split the amount into payments with different due dates. Overdue payments appear in the receivables ageing reports.\n\n## Recording payment\n\nFrom the invoice click **Create ← Payment Entry**, choose the payment method (cash or bank), and submit. The invoice is closed if the full amount is paid. Partial payment is possible, as is paying several invoices with one payment.\n\n## Advance payments\n\nIf you receive an advance payment from the Customer, record it as a Payment Entry without an invoice. When you create their invoice, the advance balance is shown and can be applied to it.\n\n## Returns\n\nFrom the submitted invoice click **Create ← Return / Credit Note**. The system reverses the revenue and the inventory by the amount of the return.\n\n## Purchase invoices\n\nThe same steps on the Supplier side: **Purchase Invoice** ← Payment Entry. It supports tax withholding and discounts.\n\n> ! Do not edit the amounts of a submitted invoice. Cancel it and recreate it, or use a return, so that the audit trail stays sound.", "journal": "A Journal Entry is the manual tool for recording any accounting transaction that other documents do not cover.\n\n## Creating an entry\n\n1. Open a new **Journal Entry** and set the date and the type (Journal Entry, Opening Entry, Depreciation...).\n2. Add the rows: account, debit or credit, and the Cost Center when needed.\n3. Make sure **total debit = total credit**.\n4. Save then submit.\n\n## When to use it\n\n- Opening balances.\n- Accrued and prepaid expenses.\n- Bank reconciliations and currency differences.\n- Correcting errors between accounts.\n\n## A row for a Customer or Supplier\n\nWhen using a receivable or payable account you must choose the **Party Type and the Party**, so that the entry appears in the party's account statement.\n\n> Entries created automatically by modules (such as payroll or reservations) are not cancelled manually. Cancel the original document and its entry will be cancelled.", "language": "## Switching language\n\nFrom **My Settings** choose the preferred language (Arabic or English). The interface and the direction change from right to left or the reverse. There is also a language switcher on the login page.\n\n## Appearance\n\nChoose light or dark mode from the user menu. This guide has a separate switch for each of language and mode at the top of the page.\n\n## Visual identity\n\nThe LedgerX logo, icons, and colors are applied to the login page, the home screen, print reports, and emails. The system administrator can change the logo from **Website Settings**.\n\n## Printing\n\nDocuments use the LedgerX print style with a light watermark. You can create your own **Print Format** for any document.\n\n## Custom fields and reports\n\n- **Custom Field**: add a new field to any document.\n- **Report Builder**: create a report from any document with filters and columns.\n- **Workflow**: add sequential approvals to documents.", "lending": "The Lending application manages customer financing with repayment schedules, interest, and collection.\n\n## The cycle\n\n1. **Loan Application**: the borrower's data, the amount, the term, and the security.\n2. **Approval**: the officer reviews the application and sets the terms.\n3. **Loan Disbursement**: creates the entry and the transfer to the borrower.\n4. **Repayment Schedule**: installments with principal and interest and due dates.\n5. **Repayment**: each installment is recorded, with the penalty calculated on late payment.\n\n## Reports\n\nOutstanding loans, overdue installments, and accrued interest.\n\n## Integration\n\nThe car showroom uses loans in the **Financing Plan** when financing is through a finance company; see the Showroom page.", "malls": "The Malls app manages a commercial mall on the same accounts, receivables and customers as the rest of LedgerX. Find it on the desktop as the **Malls** tile (route `/desk/malls`). Nothing is kept twice: rent is a Sales Invoice to the tenant's customer account, and collection is a normal Payment Entry.\n\n## Set up once\n\n1. **Mall Settings**: company, tax template, days until an invoice is due, late fee grace days and percentage, and the billing items (rent, service charge, marketing fund, utilities, turnover rent, expense recovery, late fee). The items are created for you.\n2. **Mall**: name, cost center, opening date. Then its **Floors** and **Units** (number, area, category, asking rent). A unit is Vacant, Reserved, Occupied, Fit-out or Maintenance; Occupied and Fit-out follow the lease.\n3. **Mall Tenant**: legal name, brand, tax ID, commercial register. A customer account is created for you.\n\n## Leasing: Mall Lease\n\nPick the tenant and the units, the dates and the **Rent Model**:\n\n- **Fixed Amount per Month** (or per sqm per month),\n- **Percentage of Sales**,\n- **Higher of Fixed and Percentage**: the percentage rent is billed only for the part above the fixed rent.\n\nAdd the yearly rent increase, the service charge, the marketing fund percentage, the deposit and any **Rent-free Periods** (fit-out, incentives). Two leases cannot cover the same unit on the same dates. After **Submit**, use **Terminate** or **Renew** (creates a draft renewal).\n\n## Meters, sales and visitors\n\n- **Utility Meter** and **Meter Reading**: the consumption is read against the previous reading and billed once.\n- **Tenant Sales**: monthly gross sales and returns. Sales are **Declared** until a mall manager or accountant marks them **Verified**. Turnover rent is billed only on verified sales.\n- **Footfall**: visitors per day or month, to measure sales per visitor.\n\n## Billing: Mall Billing Run\n\nChoose the mall and the month, then **Prepare Charges**: rent (with increases and free periods day by day), service charge, marketing fund, turnover rent of the previous month, unbilled meter readings, expense recovery and late fees. Review and untick lines, then **Create Invoices** (one draft Sales Invoice per lease) and **Submit Invoices**. A lease and month already invoiced is skipped.\n\n## Common-area expenses: CAM Allocation\n\nEnter the expenses to recover (or **Load Expenses** from the mall's accounts). They are shared by area times days in force; vacant space is borne by the landlord unless you untick it.\n\n## Reports\n\nRent Roll, Occupancy, Tenant Aging, Tenant Sales Performance, Lease Expiry, Footfall and Sales, Billing and Collection. Every day the app updates unit status, reminds about leases ending soon and about tenants who have not reported sales.\n\n## Roles\n\nMall Manager, Leasing Officer, Mall Accountant, Mall Operations.", "masters": "Master data is what all transactions are built on. Enter it carefully at the start.\n\n## Items\n\nFor each Item: code, name, group, unit of measure, selling and buying price, and whether it is tracked in inventory. Enable **Maintain Stock** for goods, and disable it for services.\n\n## Customers\n\n- Name, type (individual / company), Customer group, and territory.\n- Credit limit and payment terms.\n- Contacts and addresses, which can be imported with an Excel file.\n\n## Suppliers\n\nThe same idea as Customers, with payment terms, the payable account, and bank details.\n\n## Warehouses\n\nCreate a Warehouse for each physical location (branch, depot, sales representative's vehicle). Warehouses form a tree, so they can be grouped.\n\n## Price lists and taxes\n\n- A **Price List** sets the price of an Item for selling, buying, or a Customer category.\n- A **Tax Template** is added automatically to documents according to the Customer type.\n\n## Bulk import\n\nFrom the **Data Import** tool, download an Excel template, fill it in, and upload it. The system checks for errors before saving.", "payments": "Electronic payments and a network of field agents: wallets, cash custody, commissions, settlements, approvals, and a full audit log.\n\n## How money moves\n\nCompany bank ← Manager wallet ← Supervisor wallet ← Agent wallet ← the agent sells a service to the Customer and receives cash ← hands the cash to the supervisor, then to the manager, then to the company treasury.\n\n## Wallet balances\n\nEach wallet has three balances calculated from a transaction log that cannot be edited or deleted:\n\n| Balance | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| Available | The balance that services can be sold with |\n| Commission | What the agent has earned and not yet settled |\n| Cash on hand | What they have collected from Customers and not yet handed over |\n\n## Operations\n\n- **Balance transfer** between wallets according to the chain of command.\n- **Selling a service** from the agent's page on mobile, with a PIN.\n- **Cash settlement** upon handover.\n- **Refund** is a reverse operation that needs a supervisor or manager other than the requester.\n\n## Security\n\n- A balance changes only through the transaction log, with a lock that prevents spending the money twice.\n- Repeating a request with the same identifier returns the same result without a second execution.\n- A wrong PIN is counted, and the account is locked after the specified number.\n- Provider notifications are accepted only with a valid signature.\n- Entries created by the module are not cancelled manually; reverse the operation instead.\n\n## Reports\n\nPerformance of agents and supervisors, accrued commissions, open custody, and more.", "pharmacy": "The Pharmacy app runs a chain of pharmacies on the same stock, accounts, buying and HR as the rest of LedgerX. Find it on the desktop as the **Pharmacy** tile (route `/desk/pharmacy`). Nothing is kept twice: a sale is a Sales Invoice, a transfer is a Stock Entry, a purchase is a Purchase Order.\n\n## Set up once\n\n1. **Pharmacy Settings**: company, public price list, near-expiry days, whether controlled drugs need a prescription.\n2. **Pharmacy Branch**: one per branch, with its sales warehouse, an expired-stock warehouse, cost center, license and manager. Tick **Central Store** for the main store.\n3. **Item**: tick **Pharmacy Product**, then fill the class (prescription, OTC, controlled, cosmetic...), active ingredient, strength, form and **Public Price**. The item becomes batch and expiry tracked, and the price is kept in the public price list.\n4. Receive stock with a **Purchase Receipt**: each line asks for a batch number and its expiry date.\n5. **Insurance Company** (its customer account is created for you) and **Insurance Plan**: the share the insurer pays, the most and least the patient pays, and whether cosmetics are covered.\n\n## Selling: Pharmacy Dispense\n\nChoose the branch and the patient (or leave the walk-in customer), scan or pick the items. The price comes from the public price list and the screen shows the stock, the nearest expiry and a warning when a batch is close to expiry. With an insurance plan the screen shows what the patient pays and what the insurer pays.\n\nWhen you **Submit**, batches are chosen first-expiry-first-out and an expired batch is never sold. The app creates the **Sales Invoice** (stock out), the **Payment Entry** for what the patient paid and a **Journal Entry** moving the insurer's share to the insurance company's account. Cancelling the dispense cancels all three.\n\nControlled drugs need the prescription number, the doctor and the patient's national ID. This is checked on every Sales Invoice, so it also protects sales made from the normal POS. Each sale is written to the read-only **Controlled Drug Log**.\n\n## Moving stock: Pharmacy Transfer\n\n- **Branch Transfer**: from one branch to another. **Get Items > Fill from What the Branch Needs** fills what the receiving branch is short of, limited by what the sender can spare.\n- **Move to Expired Stock**: moves expired batches to the branch's expired-stock warehouse. **Fill from Expired Batches** lists them.\n- **Write Off**: removes the stock against the stock adjustment account.\n\n## Buying: Pharmacy Purchase Plan\n\nRecord the **Supplier Offer** of each company: price, discount, minimum quantity, \"buy 10 get 1 free\", dates. In the **Pharmacy Purchase Plan** choose the receiving store and press **Plan > Load Needs**: stock, orders on the way and the sales of the last days of the chosen branches are counted, and the quantity is rounded up to the pack. For every item the cheapest effective offer (free units counted) is chosen. Untick rows you do not want, then **Create Purchase Orders**: one draft order per supplier.\n\n## Chronic patients: Refill Plan\n\nA refill plan says that a patient takes a medicine every N days. The status (upcoming, due soon, overdue) moves with time, the branch manager gets a daily reminder, and every dispense of that medicine to that patient updates the plan. The **Refills Due** report is the call list.\n\n## Reports\n\n**Expiry Report**, **Drug Alternatives** (same active ingredient, price and stock), **Branch Performance**, **Controlled Drug Register**, **Insurance Receivable** (what each insurer owes, by age) and **Refills Due**.\n\n## Decision analysis\n\nThe **Analysis** menu on a branch opens Operations Research plans for it (reorder, distribution of stock to the branches). Expired stock is left out of those plans.\n\n## Limits\n\nThe calculations are covered by automated tests. Review the first invoices, payments and stock entries created by the app before relying on them, and check the insurance journal entry on the insurer's customer account.", "pos": "Point of Sale is a fast screen for shops and cashiers, working directly with inventory and accounts.\n\n## Setting up the cashier\n\n1. Create a **POS Profile** with the Warehouse, Price List, payment methods, and accounts.\n2. Specify the users allowed to use it.\n3. Open **POS Opening Entry** and enter the opening drawer balance.\n\n## Selling\n\n- Choose Items by touch or with a barcode scanner.\n- Add the Customer or sell to a cash Customer.\n- Choose the payment method (cash, card, mixed).\n- Print the receipt.\n\n## Closing the shift\n\nOn closing, the system compares the expected cash with the actual cash and shows the difference, then creates a consolidated invoice of the shift's sales.\n\n## Returns\n\nOpen the invoice and create a return, and the Item goes back to the Warehouse and the amount is refunded.\n\n## Item barcodes\n\nThe barcode scanner looks the number up in the **Barcodes** table of the Item, so every item you sell needs a barcode recorded.\n\n- Open the **Item Barcodes** page from the Item list (Menu > Item Barcodes) or at `/item-barcodes`.\n- Choose an Item Group (or All) and press **Check** to see how many items have no barcode.\n- Press **Preview** to see the numbers that would be created without changing anything, then **Create barcodes** to apply them. Each item gets an in-store EAN-13 number starting with 2 (the range reserved for shops, so it never clashes with a manufacturer's barcode), saved in the Item. Up to 1000 items per run, for Stock Managers only.\n- **Printing labels:** from the same page choose the size (62x38, 50x30, 40x25 mm or an A4 sheet), the copies and the price list; or select items in the Item list and choose **Print Barcode Labels**; or open one Item and choose **Actions > Print Barcode Label**. The label shows the item name, the barcode and the price.\n\nNotes: an item without a barcode is printed with its item code instead (it works in code search but is not a real barcode). Template items with variants get no barcode, their variants do. A barcode the supplier already gave is never replaced.", "projects": "## Project and tasks\n\nCreate a **Project** with a Customer, dates, and a budget, then divide it into **Tasks**, each assigned to someone responsible with a due date and a completion percentage.\n\n## Time tracking\n\nEmployees record work hours on tasks in the **Timesheet**, and cost and hourly billing are calculated from them.\n\n## Cost and profitability\n\nInvoices and expenses linked to the project are collected in its Cost Center. The **Project Profitability** report shows revenue, cost, and margin.\n\n## Billing\n\nBill the Customer in installments according to completion milestones, or by the recorded hours.", "realestate": "A real estate development module: from the project and units to sales, installments, contractors, handover, maintenance, and leasing.\n\n## Projects and units\n\nA project with its own Cost Center, phases, buildings, unit types, and units, with per-square-meter price lists and features added to the price (floor, view, corner...).\n\n## Sales\n\n1. **Unit reservation** with a deposit that has a validity period.\n2. **Unit contract** with a payment plan: down payment, installments, additional annual payments, handover payment, maintenance deposit.\n3. When the contract is submitted, **one invoice** is created with the payment schedule, and the payments and post-dated cheques are recorded.\n4. **Late penalties** monthly on overdue installments.\n5. **Cancellation** with a penalty, and the system reverses the invoice.\n\n## Brokers and commissions\n\nThe commission becomes due when the Customer pays a specified percentage. It is paid through a Purchase Invoice or with the salary.\n\n## Contractors and construction\n\nBill of quantities, contractor contracts, advance payments, progress certificates with retention and advance payment recovery, and construction progress for each building.\n\n## After the sale\n\n- **Handover** with a checklist and a warranty.\n- **Maintenance requests**.\n- **Owners' association** and collection of service fees.\n- **Leasing** and automatic creation of rent invoices.\n\n## Reports\n\nUnit inventory, contracts and collection, installments due, collection forecast, project profitability, and contractor certificates.\n\n## Current limits\n\n- Revenue is recognized at invoicing.\n- There is no assignment of a contract to a third party.\n- There is no property management on behalf of others.", "research": "Operations Research is a decision-support module connected to the other apps. It reads your live data (items, BOMs, stock, Work Orders, Sales Orders, Purchase requests, prices, and also vehicles from the Fleet app, asset depreciation from Assets and open deals from the CRM app) and recommends decisions and analyses questions in thirteen areas. Find it on the desktop as the **Operations Research** tile (route `/desk/operations-research`).\n\n## Common flow\n\n1. Create the plan you need and choose the **Company**.\n2. From the **Plan** menu press **Load Data**: your data is read into editable tables.\n3. Review and edit the numbers as you see fit.\n4. From **Plan** press **Solve**.\n5. Read the **Result** block: Status, **Independently Verified**, the summary and the **Read before using** list of assumptions and warnings.\n\nIf you edit the inputs after solving, the result goes back to **Draft** until you press **Solve** again.\n\nThe **Create ... (draft)** buttons create a **draft** document for you to review and submit; nothing is posted automatically. A plan that is not verified cannot create documents, and the status **Needs Attention** asks you to confirm first.\n\n## The six plans\n\n### Product Mix Plan\nWhat to make to maximise total margin under limited materials and workstation hours. You can require **whole units**. The plan shows the **value of one more unit** of each resource; the resource with the highest value is the bottleneck. Draft: **Production Plan**.\n\nAfter the plan is solved, two more buttons appear:\n\n- **What-if**: fill the table of **Scenarios**. Each row changes a resource, a product margin, a max quantity or a min quantity by a %. Rows with the same scenario name apply together. Each scenario is solved again from scratch and shows the total margin, the change against the current plan and which products change. The same button fills **Can Fall To / Can Rise To** for each bottleneck resource (the range in which the value of one more unit stays valid) and for each product margin (the range in which the plan stays the best).\n- **Risk Simulation**: margins and resources vary by the % you choose (300 simulations by default, fixed seed, so the same input gives the same answer). It shows the worst realistic, typical and best realistic total margin, in what % of cases the current plan would still be possible, and the average loss from not re-planning.\n\nEditing scenarios or risk settings does not reset the plan's result.\n\n### Reorder Plan\nComputes the ABC class, economic order quantity, safety stock for the service level you choose, the reorder point, and a next-month forecast. The forecast method is picked by back-test among moving average, exponential smoothing, trend and seasonal. Draft: **Material Request**.\n\n### Distribution Plan\nThe cheapest shipping of one item from warehouses with stock to warehouses with open transfer requests. Lane costs are entered by hand, or computed as cost per km from Address coordinates. You can block specific lanes, and unmet demand is reported. Draft: **Stock Entry** (Material Transfer).\n\n### Route Plan\nDelivery routes from open Sales Orders by vehicle capacity, with the stop order, total km, a lower bound and the % gap. Distance is straight-line, not road distance. With a vehicle list it can create draft **Fleet Trip** documents (see **Connected to the other apps**); otherwise it creates no draft.\n\n### Schedule Plan\nThe order of operations of open Work Orders on workstations, with start and end per operation. It takes the best of several dispatch rules and shows a lower bound and the gap. Working days are counted as consecutive calendar days. This plan creates no draft.\n\n### Supplier Allocation Plan\nSplits the purchase need across suppliers at least cost, respecting supplier capacity, minimum order, maximum share per supplier, longest lead time, minimum quality score, budget and a cost per extra supplier. If one supplier takes everything, it shows the extra cost if that supplier fails. Draft: **Purchase Orders**, one per supplier.\n\n## Analysis plans\n\nThese plans answer a question and create no documents. The flow is the common flow above: **Plan > Load Data** where it exists, then **Plan > Solve**, then read **Read before using**.\n\n### Break Even Analysis\nAnswers: how much must I sell to cover my costs, and how safe is my profit?\n\n- **Fixed costs** table for the period. A row can have an optional **Account** link: **Load Data** fills the amount from the ledger for the same period. Untick **Paid in Cash** for items such as depreciation.\n- **Products** table: **Load Data** reads price, cost at sale and quantity from the sales invoices of the history period. The quantities also set the sales mix.\n- Also enter the target profit and the capacity.\n- Shows: break-even units and revenue, total and per product; units and revenue for the target profit; cash break-even; margin of safety %; operating leverage; profit at expected sales; the chance of a loss and the 5% / typical / 95% profit from a risk simulation (prices, costs and volume vary by the chosen %, 2000 trials, fixed seed so the same input gives the same answer); and a sensitivity table (price, variable cost, fixed costs and volume at +/-10% and +/-20%).\n- Limits: variable cost is the stock cost at sale (add direct labour and commissions yourself); a constant sales mix is assumed; costs are linear.\n\n### Investment Analysis\nAnswers: is this investment worth its cost?\n\n- Enter the cash flows by year (year 0 = now, outflows negative) and the required return. Empty years count as zero.\n- Shows: net present value, internal rate of return, payback, discounted payback, profitability index, accept / reject, and optionally the risk (the chance that NPV is negative).\n- Note: several sign changes in the cash flows can give several IRRs; rely on the NPV.\n\n### Make or Buy Analysis\nAnswers: is it cheaper to make the item or to buy it?\n\n- Enter the yearly volume and, for making and for buying, the fixed cost and the cost per unit. **Load Data** reads the default BOM cost and the buying price.\n- Shows: the cost of each option, the cheaper option, the saving, and the volume at which both cost the same and which side is cheaper above and below it.\n\n### Lease or Buy Analysis\nAnswers: is leasing or owning cheaper over the period?\n\n- Enter the purchase price, the value at the end, the yearly running cost, the yearly lease payment, the years and the discount rate.\n- Shows: the cost of each option in today's money and the equivalent yearly cost.\n- Limits: payments are at year end; no tax or inflation.\n\n### Profitability Analysis\nAnswers: where do I really make (or lose) money?\n\n- Choose **Item**, **Customer** or **Item Group** and a period.\n- Shows: revenue, cost (stock cost at sale), margin, margin %, share of profit and a class: **A** (makes 80% of the profit), **B**, **C**, or **L** (loses money).\n- **Check Stock Health** classifies stock as **Dead / Slow / Overstocked / Healthy** from days without movement and days of cover, and shows the money tied up.\n\n### Pricing Analysis\nAnswers: what is the best price for one item?\n\n- Enter the cost, the current price and the monthly quantity, and the price elasticity. **Load Data** estimates the elasticity from 12 months of sales when the price varied enough, and shows the fit; otherwise enter your own.\n- Shows: the best price (constant-elasticity or linear demand model, within your price limits and capacity) and the profit gain. The **discount test** shows the extra volume needed to keep the same profit and the expected profit change.\n- Limit: elasticity is assumed constant near today's price.\n\n### Decision Review\nAnswers: were my earlier plans right?\n\n- It compares earlier plans with what happened: **Reorder Plan** (forecast vs the demand of the next 30 days), **Product Mix Plan** (planned vs produced quantity) and **Supplier Allocation Plan** (planned price vs the Purchase Order price).\n- Shows: average error %, bias %, tracking signal and a verdict: **Reliable**, **Usable with a buffer** or **Unreliable**.\n- Only plans old enough are checked.\n\n## Connected to the other apps\n\nOperations Research reads three more parts of LedgerX. All of these only read data and fill your tables; you can edit every number before you press **Solve**.\n\n### Fleet: vehicles in the Route Plan\n- The **Route Plan** has a new **Vehicles** table: vehicle, driver, capacity and cost per km.\n- From **Plan** press **Load Vehicles**. It reads the active vehicles from the Fleet app with their payload (kg). The cost per km is computed from the fleet's fuel logs plus the completed fleet work orders of the last 12 months, divided by the distance in the fuel logs. Driver pay, insurance and depreciation are not included. Vehicles with under 500 km of records are flagged.\n- **Load Measured In** = **Quantity** or **Weight (kg)**. Choose **Weight (kg)** when the vehicles carry payload in kg; this needs the weight on the items.\n- With a vehicle list the plan uses the cheapest vehicles that fit, and each vehicle is on at most one route. Up to 10 stops it is solved **exactly**: the best split of the stops among the vehicles and the best stop order for the cost. Beyond 10 stops it is a strong heuristic with a distance lower bound and a gap.\n- The result shows the vehicle and the cost of each route and the total cost.\n- The button **Create Fleet Trips (drafts)** creates one **draft** Fleet Trip per route: vehicle, driver, origin (the depot), destination (the last stop), distance, cargo weight when the plan is weight-based, and a description listing the stops in order. Review each trip before you use it.\n- Without a vehicle list the earlier mode with identical vehicles still works. Distances are straight-line.\n\n### Assets\n- **Lease or Buy Analysis**: choose an **Existing Asset** and press **Plan > Load Data**. It fills the purchase price, the value at the end and the years from the asset's depreciation settings. It also shows the book value, the remaining depreciation years and the depreciation per year, for information only. The comparison uses the cost of a **new** asset, because depreciation is not a cash flow.\n- **Break Even Analysis**: tick **Add Asset Depreciation of the Period**. Then **Load Data** adds the scheduled depreciation of the active asset schedules in the history period as a fixed cost row that is **not paid in cash**. So it counts in the break-even but not in the cash break-even.\n\n### CRM: expected demand from deals\n- In the **Reorder Plan** and the **Product Mix Plan** tick **Add Expected Demand From CRM Deals**.\n- It reads the open deals (not Won or Lost) of the CRM app that close within the horizon: in the Reorder Plan the field **CRM Horizon (days)** (default 90), in the Product Mix Plan the planning days. It takes the products of those deals and weights each quantity by the deal probability: the deal's own probability, else its status probability, else the default in **OR Settings** (30%).\n- **Reorder Plan**: the quantity per item is shown in **Expected From CRM Deals** and is added to the yearly demand as a yearly rate (quantity x 365 / horizon). Items that appear only in deals are included.\n- **Product Mix Plan**: the expected quantity is added to the demand cap of each product, together with the open Sales Orders.\n- These quantities are expectations, not orders. Deals without a closing date are counted and flagged.\n\n## Coordinates\n\n**Address** has new fields **Latitude** and **Longitude**. Routes and distribution need them: customers through their address, warehouses through an address linked to the warehouse.\n\n## Roles\n\n**Research Manager** and **Research Analyst**.\n\n## Honest limits\n\n- Results are optimal **for your data and the model**, and the model is a simplification of reality.\n- Product mix, supplier allocation and shipping use exact methods.\n- Routes and scheduling are strong heuristics that show a lower bound and a gap; this is not a proof of optimality.\n- Forecasts are statistical and come with an error warning.\n- Wrong input gives wrong output, so always read the **Read before using** list.\n- Every result is re-checked by independent code (feasibility, and for linear problems an optimality certificate) before it is called verified.\n- Risk simulations assume independent normal variation of each input; real inputs often move together.\n- The review depends on the age of the plans: a recent plan cannot be checked yet.\n- The CRM link depends on the deals having products and probabilities; deals without them add nothing or fall back to the default probability.\n- The fleet cost per km is only as good as the fuel records, and it leaves out driver pay, insurance and depreciation.\n- Route distances are straight-line, not road distances.\n- Every new analysis states a **Read before using** list: read it before you rely on the result.\n> ! The tool supports your decision, it does not replace it: review the draft before you submit it.\n\n## Pharmacy chains\n\nWhen the Pharmacy app is installed:\n\n- **Expired stock is never counted as stock on hand.** The Reorder Plan and the Distribution Plan leave expired batches out and warn you how many units were excluded.\n- **Distribution Plan > Add Needs of Pharmacy Branches**: before **Load Data**, tick it and each branch's need (from its recent sales, its minimum level and its sellable stock) is added as a destination. If a transfer request already exists for the same warehouse, the larger of the two is used, never both.\n- On a **Pharmacy Branch**, the **Analysis** menu opens a Reorder Plan for that branch, or a Distribution Plan for the needs of all branches.", "selling": "## The sales cycle\n\nQuotation ← Sales Order ← Delivery Note ← Sales Invoice ← Payment Entry.\n\nYou can start from any step; you do not have to go through all of them.\n\n## Quotation\n\nIt is sent to the Customer with prices, terms, and a validity date. On approval click **Create ← Sales Order**.\n\n## Sales Order\n\nIt fixes the quantities, prices, and delivery date, and reserves the goods in inventory. It shows what has been delivered and what has been invoiced.\n\n## Delivery and invoice\n\n- The **Delivery Note** takes the goods out of the Warehouse.\n- The **Invoice** records the revenue and the receivable.\n- You can enable **Update Stock** in the invoice to combine the two steps.\n\n## Prices and discounts\n\n- Price Lists for each Customer category.\n- Pricing rules apply discounts by quantity, Item, or Customer.\n- The credit limit prevents selling to a Customer who has exceeded their limit.\n\n## Sales reports\n\nSales by Customer, Item, and sales representative, pending orders, and overdue collection.", "showroom": "A new and used car showroom: one showroom or several: inventory, transfers between branches, reservation, sales, financing, and sales representative commissions.\n\n## The car cycle\n\n1. **Entering the Warehouse**: the purchase is posted to inventory.\n2. **Preparation**: a checklist and extra expenses that are added to the car's cost.\n3. **Readiness**: the car passes through the states Draft, In Preparation, Ready, Reserved, Sold, Delivered.\n4. **Reservation**: a deposit recorded on the Customer's account.\n5. **Sale**: **Car Sale** creates the invoice, the cost of sale, and the margin.\n6. **Delivery**: the car leaves the Warehouse.\n\n## Financing plans\n\nDefine a **Financing Plan** once and apply it to the sales contract:\n\n| Type | Description |\n|---|---|\n| Showroom installments | Direct installments from the showroom over a number of months with a profit percentage |\n| Bank or finance company | The financier pays the price of the car, and the Customer pays them in installments |\n| Loan | Linked to the Lending module |\n\nWhen the plan is chosen, the installment term, the financier, the profit percentage, and the minimum down payment are filled in, and the **installment schedule** appears in the sales contract. The invoice carries the installments as a payment schedule.\n\n## Connections\n\nFrom the Customer, employee, invoice, or Journal Entry you will find a **Connections** panel that opens the linked sales contracts and reservations.\n\n## Customers and commissions\n\nLeads can be linked to cars and test drives recorded, and the sales representative's commission is calculated monthly and goes into payroll.\n\n## Reports\n\nShowroom inventory, car sales margin, and installments due.\n\n> The showroom works with a single currency.", "start": "## First steps\n\n1. **Log in** with your email and password from the system's home page.\n2. **Create the company** and set the currency and the Fiscal Year (see the Company and Fiscal Year page).\n3. **Review the Chart of Accounts** and adjust it to your business.\n4. **Add users** and give them the appropriate Roles.\n5. **Enter the master data**: Items, Customers, Suppliers, Warehouses.\n6. **Create your first invoice** and review its effect on the accounts.\n\n## Tips for getting started\n\n- Try everything on test data before entering real balances.\n- Enter the opening balances in a single Journal Entry dated the start of the Fiscal Year.\n- Enable only the modules you need, and don't rush to turn everything on.\n\n## Using search\n\nPress `Ctrl + K` inside the system to search for any document, report, or page by name.\n\n> If an error appears, copy its full text and check the **FAQ** page or contact the system administrator.", "stock": "## Stock movement\n\nEvery movement is made through a **Stock Entry**: receipt, issue, transfer between Warehouses, manufacturing. They are also created automatically from commercial documents (invoice, receipt, delivery).\n\n## Balances\n\nThe **Stock Balance** report shows the quantity and value for each Item and Warehouse. The **Stock Ledger** shows all movements.\n\n## Tracking\n\n- **Serial Number**: for Items where each piece is tracked.\n- **Batch**: for Items that have a production or expiry date.\n\n## Stock counting\n\nUse **Stock Reconciliation** to enter the actual quantities. The system calculates the differences and posts an adjustment entry for their value.\n\n## Inventory valuation\n\nThe valuation method is set (Moving Average or FIFO). The value is reflected automatically in the stock account and the cost of goods sold.\n\n## Reorder level\n\nSet a minimum level and a reorder quantity for each Item, and the system creates a **Material Request** when stock drops.\n\n> ! A negative balance usually indicates a sales invoice made before the purchase receipt. Disable it from Stock Settings if you want to prevent it.", "store": "The Store app is an online store and a website that run on the same stock, prices, customers, orders and invoices as the rest of LedgerX. Find its management screens on the desktop as the **Store** tile (route `/desk/store`). Customers use the public pages: `/store`, `/shop`, `/cart`, `/checkout`, `/my-orders`, `/news`, `/contact-us`.\n\n## Set up once\n\n1. **Store Settings**: store name and colors, the company, the price list, the warehouses that fill online orders, the shipping fee (with its income account), the payment methods and your contact details.\n2. **Item Group**: tick *Show in the Online Store* on the categories to show.\n3. **Item**: tick *Show in the Online Store* on every product. A product needs a price in the store price list and stock in the chosen warehouses (or *Sell even when out of stock*). Tick *Feature on the Home Page* to put it first.\n4. To make the store the home page of the website, tick that option in Store Settings.\n\n## Orders\n\nA customer adds products to the cart and checks out as a guest or signed in. The app creates or reuses the **Customer**, **Contact** and **Address**, then makes a **Sales Order**, and the order page shows its status. Your team gets a task for each new order. From there the normal flow applies: Delivery Note, Sales Invoice, Payment Entry. Prices, stock and tax are checked again on the server when the order is placed, so an old cart cannot sell something that is gone.\n\n## Payment\n\n- **Cash on delivery**.\n- **Bank transfer or wallet**: the customer sees your instructions. When the money arrives press **Store > Record Payment** on the Sales Order: it creates the Payment Entry.\n- **Online payment** through Paymob: the order is marked paid only when the signed callback arrives and the amount matches. Online orders not paid within 24 hours are marked Failed.\n\n## Pharmacy, cars and rooms\n\nOver-the-counter pharmacy products can be sold; prescription and controlled drugs never are, and expired batches are not counted in stock. Cars (ready for sale) can be shown with a **test drive** request that creates the showroom's Test Drive and a Lead. Hotel rooms can be shown with a **booking request** that creates a Lead; your team confirms availability.\n\n## Website\n\n**Store Page** holds pages you write (about, services, policies) and can show them in the menu. **Store Post** holds the news you write; published posts show under News. The contact form creates a **Store Inquiry** and a lead in the CRM (a CRM Lead when the CRM app is installed).\n\n## Important\n\nThe store is tested with simulated data. Place test orders and run a Paymob test payment on a copy of the site before opening it to customers.", "users": "## Adding a user\n\n1. Open **User** and add a new user by email.\n2. Enter the name and the preferred language.\n3. From the **Roles** tab, select what they need (Accountant, Sales Manager, Stock Keeper...).\n4. Save, and the user receives a link to set their password.\n\n## Roles\n\nA Role is a set of permissions: read, write, create, delete, submit, export. A user can be given more than one Role. From the **Role Permissions Manager** you set what each Role can do on each document type.\n\n## Restricting data (User Permissions)\n\nTo restrict a user to a specific branch, Warehouse, or company, add a **User Permission** for them, and they will see only the records linked to it. This is very useful in multi-branch companies.\n\n## Account security\n\n- Use strong passwords, and enable two-factor authentication for managers.\n- Disable an employee's account when they leave instead of deleting it, so the record of their operations remains.\n- Review the **Activity Log** to see who changed what and when.\n\n> ! Do not share the manager account between more than one person, as this undermines auditing.", "what": "LedgerX is an integrated business management system that brings accounting, sales, purchasing, inventory, human resources, and customer management together in one place, with a full Arabic interface and English when you need it.\n\n## What the system does\n\nLedgerX records everything that happens in your company: from the quotation and the invoice, to payment and inventory, to payroll and the accounting entry. Every transaction is reflected in the accounts automatically. There is no need to enter data twice.\n\n## Who uses it\n\n- **Small and medium businesses** that want one system instead of several separate programs.\n- **Multi-branch companies** that need Cost Centers and permissions for each branch.\n- **Specialized businesses**: hotels, car showrooms, schools and universities, real estate development, transport and fleet companies, and electronic payment networks.\n\n## System components\n\n| Part | Function |\n|---|---|\n| Accounting core | Accounts, invoices, payments, taxes, reports |\n| Sales, purchasing, and inventory | The complete trade cycle from order to delivery |\n| Customer management | Leads, opportunities, follow-up |\n| Human resources | Employees, attendance, leave, payroll |\n| Lending | Customer financing and repayment schedules |\n| LedgerX modules | Fleet, field sales, payment network, hotels, showroom, education, real estate |\n\n> Every module works with the others: a showroom invoice, a real estate contract, or a student fee appears in the customer's accounts and consolidated reports.", "why": "## One system instead of several programs\n\nWhen data is scattered across an accounting program, an inventory program, and Excel sheets, reports are delayed and numbers conflict. In LedgerX every department reads from a single database, so the figure the accountant sees is the same one the sales manager sees.\n\n## Fully Arabic\n\nThe interface, printing, and reports all work right to left, and the accounting terms are clear Arabic terms. Each user can switch the language to English at any time.\n\n## Grows with you\n\n- Start with accounts and invoices only, then enable inventory and human resources when you need them.\n- Add new branches and companies without rebuilding the system.\n- Enable specialized modules according to your business without affecting the rest of the system.\n\n## Open and customizable\n\nYou can add fields, reports, and permissions specific to your company from within the system, without programming in most cases.\n\n## Reasonable cost of ownership\n\nIt runs on your own server or your own hosting, and your data stays with you."};
